{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/30201-refinements-as-anchors","id":30201,"title":"Refinements as Anchors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-14T18:57:13-08:00","id":30201,"title":"Refinements as Anchors","content":"So, this is coming out from some discussions across fora old an new. The idea takes a page from Blood &amp; Smoke, abandoning Virtue and Vice for Masquerade and Requiem, to represent the new priorities of the vampire. As a reminder, Masquerade is the mortal persona the vampire maintains or adopts, and Requiem is the true, monstrous face of the vampire among its Kindred.<br /> <br /> Obviously Masquerade and Requiem don't mesh well with the Promethean: there isn't really a role among mortals he can hold on to, nor one among the Created that he can draw comfort from. Yet neither does Virtue and Vice, not if you examine Prometheans as half-formed naifs grasping at humanity. In some of my conversations, the idea was discussed that Virtues and Vices needed to be earned, that a Promethean doesn't spring into life so developed that he has enough identity to draw comfort from it. <br /> <br /> Into this void, the idea came that Refinement, as a conduit to humanity, might offer a proxy self-image. A Titan could draw strength from believing himself strong, a Muse could inspire herself by convincing herself of her ability to pass as human. In time, as a Promethean came to know himself, he could learn a Vice, then a Virtue, and then, accepting the flaws and strengths of a human, could ore readily enter Mortality.<br /> <br /> Anyway, enough prelude, I have the basics for how Refinements could be used as a starting Anchor for Prometheans to gain Willpower in the absence of Virtue and Vice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b> Cuprum as an Anchor</b></td> </tr> </table></div> Sample Aspirations</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Find a lair in the densest neighborhood of the city.</li> <li>Enjoy a moment of engagement with a wild animal.</li> <li>Turn a foe into an ally.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Willpower Rewards (&quot;Vice&quot;)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Gain a point of Willpower when a dilemma affecting you is resolved by your inaction.</li> <li>Gain a point of Willpower when you successfully hide from pursuers.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Major Willpower Rewards (&quot;Virtue&quot;)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Regain all spent Willpower when you retreat from a situation that can harm your friends.</li> <li>Regain all spent Willpower when you turn an enemy into an ally.</li> </ul></span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b>Centimanus as an Anchor</b><br /></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Aspirations</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Capture a Pandoran.</li> <li>Create a Praecipitatus.</li> <li>Find the purpose of Flux in the Pilgrimage.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Willpower Rewards (&quot;Vice&quot;)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Command a Pandoran effectively.</li> <li>Be reviled as a monster, either by humans or your own kind.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Major Willpower Rewards (&quot;Virtue&quot;)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Regain all spent Willpower when you feed a Pandoran without sacrificing your own flesh.</li> <li>Regain all spent Willpower when you consciously commit an act that forces a degeneration roll (automatic Humanity loss does not qualify).</li> </ul></span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b>Stannum as an Anchor</b><br /></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Aspirations</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Get your revenge, be it petty or deserved.</li> <li>Wrest a sincere apology from one who has wronged you.</li> <li>Achieve an Aspiration while in Torment</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Willpower Rewards (&quot;Vice&quot;)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Inflict another with a Condition that applies a penalty.</li> <li>Mock or worsen another's suffering.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Major Willpower Rewards (&quot;Virtue&quot;)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Inflict a persistent Condition on yourself or another.</li> <li>Alienate an ally while still benefiting from his aid.</li> </ul></span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b>Mercurius as an Anchor</b><br /></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Aspirations</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Discover a new use for Pyros.</li> <li>Learn a non-Affinity Transmutation</li> <li>Witness an unmoored human soul.</li> </ul></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Willpower Rewards (&quot;Vice&quot;)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Gain a point of Willpower when you spark or witness a massive exchange of energy.</li> <li>Gain a point of Willpower when you uncover the existence of an unfamiliar Promethean.</li> </ul></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Major Willpower Rewards (&quot;Virtue&quot;)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Regain all spent Willpower when your use of Pyros drives a mortal into end-stage Disquiet.</li> <li>Regain all spent Willpower when you or your throng are caught in a Firestorm or a qashmallim's Mission.</li> </ul></span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b>Ferrum as an Anchor</b><br /></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Aspirations</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Prove the strength of your body or will.</li> <li>Defeat an enemy in a fair fight.</li> <li>Survive an ordeal that is lethal to mortals.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Willpower Rewards</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Gain a Willpower point when you overcome an obstacle that has defeated you before.</li> <li>Gain a Willpower point when you convince an adversary to fight on your terms.</li> </ul></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Major Willpower Rewards</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Regain all spent Willpower when you defeat an opponent on his own terms.</li> <li>Regain all spent Willpower when you achieve a physical aim without benefitting from Pyros or Transmutation use.</li> </ul></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <b>Aurum as an Anchor</b><br /></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Aspirations</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Be accepted into a church congregation, community theater group, or some other tight-knit group.</li> <li>Flaunt a symbol of status or esteem, such as a luxury car or a gang tattoo.</li> <li>Use your position to ingratiate your throngmates into a mortal social circle.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Minor Willpower Rewards (&quot;Vice&quot;)</span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Gain a Willpower point when you refuse to aid to your social lesser.</li> <li>Gain a Willpower point when you indulge in group activities without questioning their value.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Major Willpower Rewards (&quot;Virtue&quot;)</span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><ul><li>Regain all spent Willpower when you suffer injury or loss on behalf of another.</li> <li>Regain all spent Willpower when you are offered or granted a position of respect in a mortal institution or society.</li> </ul></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T14:52:23-08:00","id":30596,"title":"","content":"I enjoy this, and I enjoy the idea.<br /> I like the connection between Prometheans having Virtues + Vices, and Pandorans only having Vices, and so this makes me both pensive and wary.<br /> Virtues and Vices are super-cool for Prometheans, but working towards them is also, obviously, great.<br /> <br /> Right now, under my own hacks, when you resolve a Beacon you get a Breaking Point.<br /> Do you think we could combine that with your Remnant: when you resolve your first Beacon, you get Virtue or Vice, and when you resolve your Remnant, you get the other?<br /> + some Vitriol, of course.<br /> <br /> Too complex/just right? For some reason, building Breaking Points seems fine to me, but building Virtue + Vice in-game seems to push the complexity scale.<br /> I think that's just because I've been playing White Wolf for so long that the &quot;Nature/Demeanor&quot; equivalents not being something you start with and basically always have is toying with my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T19:52:31-08:00","id":32101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think we could combine that with your Remnant: when you resolve your first Beacon, you get Virtue or Vice, and when you resolve your Remnant, you get the other?<br /> + some Vitriol, of course. </div> </div> </div>Possibly. My notion with the Remnant is that <i>how</i> you resolve it matters. If you basically accept it, succumb to it, whatever, then what you get in return is a Vice. You get Willpower when you sate <i>its</i> needs, when you sublimate it. When you reject it, or parse it down to your own benefit, or reclaim it as your own, you've established yourself as a being of rational, conscious thought, and gain a Virtue as your reward.<br /> <br /> Now, that puts design in a weird space, because the assumption is that Virtue and Vice are functional opposite halves, and if they resolve from separate things, then resolving the first locks the second into its counterpart. So, if the Promethean resolves his Remnant into a Virtue, then Trait B intuitively must resolve into a Vice. Now, we can be progressive, and ditch the idea of one Vice to one Virtue, but that seems to leave us with a incomplete creature on par with an angel. We can leave that second anchor &quot;locked in&quot;, and treat the arc between the resolution of the first and the resolution of the second as a part of the Pilgrimage, but is that a workable solution, and does that subtract agency from the equation?<br /> <br /> Hmm, I just realized I need to make the Remnant a Willpower generator if it's to function as a substitute anchor. Which is fair, but grr for the oversight.<br /> <br /> Any feedback on the particulars in the original post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}